2026-06-06 12:11:06,458 TITLE: Anaerobic bioprocessing of wastewater-derived duckweed: Maximizing product yields in a biorefinery value cascade Title of processing article
2026-06-06 12:12:32,713 {
  "pretreatments": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "description": "Liquid hot water pretreatment was carried out in a 500 ml stainless steel Parr reactor with a pressure limit of 345 bar. The vessel was filled with 30 g duckweed (dry weight) and 270 g distilled water. The temperature was ramped up to 150 °C within 15 min, followed by pressurization with nitrogen gas for 5 min. This chemical-thermal treatment affects substrate properties, including enzymatic activity and hydrolysis."
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "description": "Prior to liquefaction, the duckweed was sterilized by autoclaving with 945 ml water for 30 min at 121 °C. This thermal treatment removes microorganisms and affects the substrate's microbial composition and enzymatic potential."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "description": "Enzymatic liquefaction and saccharification of the duckweed was performed in four 2-L flasks with 1 L total working volume. Prior to liquefaction, the duckweed was sterilized by autoclaving. pH was adjusted to 7.0 ± 0.1 with 2 M hydrochloric acid. α-amylase (5000 units g starch^-1) was added at 90 °C, followed by glucoamylase and cellulase. Saccharification was performed at 50 °C while mixing at 120 rpm for 24 h. This enzymatic-chemical treatment converts substrates into fermentable sugars, affecting substrate solubility and composition."
    }
  ]
}
